# Keep the build context small and keep secrets out of the image.
#
# Everything listed here is either useless in the image or actively unwanted.
# A large context is slow to send to the daemon and every file in it is a file
# that could accidentally be COPYed in.

# Build output — the image builds its own inside stage 1. There is deliberately
# no negation re-including target/*.jar: nothing here COPYs a host-built JAR, and
# a 71MB stale one in the context would only be dead weight the daemon has to
# read and a file a careless `COPY . .` could pick up ahead of the real build.
target/

# The Maven wrapper is for humans and CI, not for the image. The build stage
# starts FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21, which already pins Maven, so copying
# the wrapper in would only make the build download a second copy of the same
# version. Excluding it also stops a `COPY . .` from ever shadowing that.
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd

# VCS and IDE
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Docs and infrastructure: not needed to run the app
*.md
k8s/
cluster.yaml
template.yaml
.github/
lambda/
events/
# The build recipe itself is not an input to the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Anything that could carry credentials
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
**/secret.yaml
